  "configuration_id": "config_039",
  "reason": "The current best configuration (config_037: multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, ViT-L, avgpool, weighted; acc 0.706) has only been tested with avgpool aggregation. The prior evidence from PCA-2000 (config_002 vs config_003) showed transformer underperforming avgpool by ~0.07, but that comparison used linear 2000-dim features; scvi_n200 produces learned, nonlinear 200-dim latent features that may interact differently with attention-based aggregation. Config_039 changes only the aggregation from avgpool to transformer while holding all other variables (scvi_n200, ViT-L, multiprofile, weighted fusion) fixed, providing a clean single-variable test of whether transformer aggregation can improve upon the current best. If it succeeds, it directly extends the best configuration; if it fails, it confirms avgpool is robustly optimal across encoder types and frees budget to explore other dimensions. This is the most efficient exploitation step given the strong evidence for the current configuration and the one remaining untested aggregation variant in the best-performing setup."
}

